  "mathematicalIdentityOverReals": "For e=y-P and c=R-P: |e-c|<|e| iff c*(2*e-c)>0; equivalently e and c have the same nonzero sign and 0<|c|<2*|e|.",
  "tiesOverReals": "c=0 always ties; if c is nonzero, equality occurs exactly at c=2*e. When e=0, every nonzero correction loses.",
  "overshootMeaning": "A correction may pass the target and still help if it does not reach twice the true displacement. Overshooting is not by itself a loss.",
  "binary64Boundary": "Outcomes here are from direct errors abs(y-P) and abs(y-R), using the frozen stored binary64 values. Symbolic identities are over reals; product/expanded identities were never used to route or score. Mechanism bin boundaries use e=y-P and c=R-P and binary64 comparisons; near exact boundaries rounding may matter.",
  "physicalInterpretationLimit": "Unchanged published target means the stored target equals P, not proof of physically constant oxygen, sensor accuracy, or a causal source of failure. Target displacement categories are only observable after the forecast.",
